          "inline_source_record": {
            "id": "S6",
            "published_at": "2026-10-28",
            "publisher": "Microsoft",
            "tier": "T0",
            "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
          },
          "original_source_id": "S6",
          "original_source_record": {
            "document_version": "live official transcript as retrieved; no historical version reconstruction",
            "event_at": "2026-10-28",
            "first_retrieved_at": "2026-10-31T17:18:42.048Z",
            "fiscal_period": "FY27 Q1",
            "id": "S6",
            "local_text": "source-material/S6/page.txt",
            "period_end": "2026-09-30",
            "period_start": "2026-07-01",
            "published_at": "2026-10-28",
            "publisher": "Microsoft",
            "quotes": [
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L209",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:209",
                "quote": "Accelerating demand led to us adding 24 new data centers across five continents this quarter.",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L259",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:259",
                "quote": "In closing, based on the demand we see, the strength of our products, and the efficiencies we are driving across the stack, I have never been more confident in the long-term returns on our investments.",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L269",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:269",
                "quote": "Operating expenses increased 6%, driven by continued investments in R&D compute capacity and talent. Operating margins increased slightly year-over-year to 50%, driven by strong revenue growth, platform efficiency gains, and focused investments across our portfolio, partially offset by sales mix shift to Azure.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L273",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:273",
                "quote": "Capital expenditures were $45.2 billion, as some third-party capacity deliveries we expected in Q1 were delayed. Roughly three quarters of our capex was for short-lived assets, primarily CPUs and GPUs, including higher memory and storage costs, as we continue to invest in the infrastructure required for our customers to build and scale AI applications.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L275",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:275",
                "quote": "The remaining spend was for long-lived assets. This quarter, finance leases were $7.4 billion. As a reminder, we recognize the full principal value of finance leases in capex at the time of lease commencement. And cash paid for P, P, and E was $39.4 billion.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L277",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:277",
                "quote": "Cash flow from operations was $58 billion, up 29% driven by strong cloud billings and collections. And free cash flow was $18.6 billion reflecting higher capital expenditures.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L279",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:279",
                "quote": "And finally, we returned $10.2 billion to shareholders through dividends and share repurchases.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L281",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:281",
                "quote": "Now, to our segment results, reported under the updated segment structure announced in September.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L287",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:287",
                "quote": "Commercial remaining performance obligation grew 73% to $677 billion, with a smaller sequential decline relative to historical seasonality due to the large Azure commitment this quarter. ",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L289",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:289",
                "quote": "Our RPO has a weighted average duration of 2.3 years. And roughly 30% will be recognized in revenue in the next 12 months, up 29% year-over-year. The remaining portion recognized beyond the next 12 months increased 98%.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L291",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:291",
                "quote": "Now to Microsoft Cloud. Revenue was $63.9 billion and growth accelerated to 30% and 31% in constant currency, with sequential dollars added nearly doubling year-over-year, reflecting strong demand across Azure and M365 Commercial cloud.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L293",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:293",
                "quote": "Azure revenue was ahead of expectations and increased 48%, even with the 3P capacity delays noted earlier, driven by Foundry and improved CPU monetization. Foundry revenue more than tripled year-over-year with upside driven by efficiency gains across our GPU fleet that allowed us to allocate additional capacity to customers, as well as higher revenue per token that we benefited from in the quarter. Across our CPU fleet, engineering work enabled us to identify and monetize underutilized capacity this quarter, helping us serve more of the growing demand with our existing capacity. The timing of engineering efficiencies like these as well as 3P GPU lease deliveries, our own capacity build outs, and ARPU changes from model mix, can create quarterly variability in the year-over-year growth rate.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L305",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:305",
                "quote": "Microsoft Cloud gross margin percentage declined year-over-year to 66%, driven by sales mix shift to Azure, partially offset by product-level margin improvements, primarily in Azure.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L329",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:329",
                "quote": "In Azure, we expect revenue growth of 49 to 50% in constant currency with continued efficiency gains across our CPU and GPU fleet helping to offset some 3P GPU as a service contracts that have been delayed to H2. Customer demand continues to exceed available supply. And looking beyond Q2, year-over-year growth will continue to reflect the timing and scale of engineering efficiencies delivered in the quarter, and new capacity adds, as well as a strong prior-year comparable that included accelerating growth in the second half.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L341",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:341",
                "quote": "Microsoft Cloud gross margin percentage should be roughly 65%, down year-over-year as continued improvement in product-level margins is more than offset by sales mix shift to Azure.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L361",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:361",
                "quote": "In Q2, we expect CapEx spend will be over $50 billion. Therefore, for the calendar year, spend should be approximately $170 billion due to the 3P capacity delays noted earlier. In the second half of the fiscal year, we currently expect CapEx spend to accelerate primarily from CPUs, inclusive of higher memory and storage costs, and GPUs, as well as the 3P capacity deliveries that shifted to H2. And as we continue to improve the efficiency of our infrastructure, each dollar of capex has the potential to support more revenue and higher returns over time.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L363",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:363",
                "quote": "Given our strong business performance, we expect to continue to remain free cash flow positive in FY27. To complement cash generated by the business and preserve financial flexibility, we will access additional sources of funding when we believe it is attractive to do so.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L379",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:379",
                "quote": "SATYA NADELLA: Thanks for the question, Adam. I’d say all of the above, but I think the way we’re coming at this is we have one pool, and we want to get the pool to be as efficient and fungible. That’s the place where, if I think about all of the physics of how we’re building out the data centers, all the operational rigor with which we can bring up the capacity, and then, of course, how do we run the workloads that are optimized on our infrastructure?",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L381",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:381",
                "quote": "And once you do that, then it’s just a function of how we allocate it by looking at the demand signal. And even there, even in our new segment reporting, I think you kind of see it, which is Copilot, Copilot stateful database underneath it is Work IQ. That gets used in Foundry, which is where people will build, let’s say, a multi-agent system for supply chain that spans both unstructured and structured. Of course, it uses a Postgres database in Azure. And then, by the way, all the agentic work is registered in the Agent 365, and Perception manages the security of it.",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L383",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:383",
                "quote": "To us, at least, we look at all of this as the same infrastructure. Of course, we report to you in a variety of different products, but your core question of where is the margin going to come from, where is the leverage going to come from, it’s going to come from every one of them. And it compounds when we work them across.",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L405",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:405",
                "quote": "Those efficiencies, they’re ground out every week. And you have good ideas; a lot work, some don’t, and you stay at it. They’re not maybe as predictable in terms of how much impact we’ll get in quarter. Q1, they did a very good job, and you saw some of that result in us being able to put more allocation into Foundry in the quarter.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L409",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:409",
                "quote": "Secondly, and you mentioned it, token pricing will create a little bit of variability. We had higher token pricing than we expected in the quarter. Listen, high quality models that we’re able to take advantage of and see good margins on do benefit us in the quarter. That did happen in Q1.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L413",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:413",
                "quote": "In Q2 we’ve got those efficiency gains, which is great, and those will continue into Q2. We need to find some more, which we’re counting on, enable to get to that guidance that I gave because I have faith in the teams who work in Q1 continuing into Q2. But we also need that work to be able to help us a little bit because we had some supply we were counting on Q2 move out into H2.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L415",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:415",
                "quote": "And so, I think, and to your point, there’s also some unknown on some token pricing through the quarter. That stuff can change.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L443",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:443",
                "quote": "And so, in that sense, the enterprise breadth motion is starting, but like everything else, the enterprise stuff is not a quarter over quarter. It’s a decade-long thing, and that’s what I’ve been waiting for, as opposed to four customers who buy a lot of capacity from you, and you can show a few quarters of growth. And that’s not a business, as far as I’m concerned.",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L445",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:445",
                "quote": "I want the breadth. We are well positioned on the breadth, and we have large customers who want to buy from us. And we’re open for business with it. And as long as the pricing is right, we may sell them some. If not, we will be patient about building the breadth business.",
                "speaker": "SATYA NADELLA",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L525",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:525",
                "quote": "AMY HOOD: Great. I’ll take that. I think what I said is, if it’s attractive and makes sense. We’re lucky; we have a lot of flexibility in terms of our capacity to raise financing. I’ve talked about this before. There’s a form of financing called leasing, and we’ve been using that one as a vehicle. Also, we’re fortunate to have access in the debt markets, given that where our ratings are, and we haven’t been able to, and we haven’t yet, I would say, tap that.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              },
              {
                "context": "prepared remarks or Q&A; see surrounding lines",
                "date": "2026-10-28",
                "id": "S6-L527",
                "locator": "source-material/S6/page.txt:527",
                "quote": "And then, of course, there’s other options, but I think the way I see it is we’re feeling good that we’re free cash flow positive. We feel good that the return on every dollar of CapEx we’re spending, we’re confident in that. And therefore, we feel like we have lots of options to be able to tap the financing markets when they make sense and they’re attractive.",
                "speaker": "AMY HOOD",
                "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2027/earnings-fy-2027-q1"
              }
            ],
